From a1fa28da546f34ed96becca613aeac6f2bfc2a65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:53:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): the cut list or the nesting of a saved .shz as
 JSON, headless

Issue #14 asked for a way to read a cut list from a .shz as JSON
without opening the app. sawhorse-cli (crates/cli, a new workspace
crate) does that and the nesting: `sawhorse-cli cutlist Bookshelf.shz`
prints what the Cut list pane reads, `sawhorse-cli nest Bookshelf.shz`
what the Nesting section reads, with --visible-only, --rounding
sixteenth|thirty-second|half-mm (cutlist) and --pretty. It is the
kernel's own serialization through sawhorse_shz::read, so a file gives
the same JSON here and in the app, hash included. No dependency beyond
the kernel, the reader and serde; it reads and prints, never writes;
builds for wasm32 like every workspace crate. Building or changing a
model from the command line, and an MCP server, are left for later.

Tests: crates/cli/tests/cutlist.rs (a saved board's cut list and
nesting equal the kernel's for the same model, byte for byte; rounding
and visible-only reach the kernel; a file that is not a document says
so; the command line end to end: every option, every refusal, a
missing file). Smoke-tested on a .shz saved by the 0.1.0-alpha.4 app.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DaoaGXWjtprTCuXM54m2KR
